    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d601">

                <pb facs="0783" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg689"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Taylor.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-16"><hi rendition="#italic">October 16,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Consul-general at Habana cables that General Weyler declares he has received no
                    information nor instructions from his Government about tobacco of Americans
                    purchased or contracted for before decree prohibiting exportation. See minister
                    for foreign affairs at once and ask for explicit and immediate cable
                    instructions to Weyler.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
